# A file of instance data (an A-box), and what OntoCanvas shows for it (issues #181 and #168).
#
# The graph draws classes, so it shows one node here, :Room, the only class the file declares. The four individuals,
# and the classes :Door and :Wall that they use without declaring them, are not drawn. Expected:
#   - the bottom bar shows "issues (1)"; its popup says "4 individuals" are not drawn, and links the issues that track
#     drawing instance data;
#   - the SPARQL panel's starting query lists the individuals with their classes (it lists classes for a file without
#     individuals): four rows, :door1 :Door / :room1 :Room / :room2 :Room / :wallA :Wall;
#   - this query shows the links between them: SELECT ?a ?b WHERE { ?a :hasDoor ?b } ORDER BY ?a -> :room1 :door1 and :room2 :door1.
@prefix : <http://example.org/examples/instance-data#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/examples/instance-data> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Instance data example" .

:Room a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Room" .

:room1 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room one" ; :hasDoor :door1 .
:room2 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room two" ; :hasDoor :door1 .
:door1 a :Door ; rdfs:label "Door" .
:wallA a :Wall ; rdfs:label "Wall A" .
